{"title":"Add slugify() helper for URL-friendly slugs","body":"Adds an exported `slugify(input: string): string` to `src/index.ts` that normalizes a string into a URL-friendly slug: lowercased and trimmed, with every run of non-alphanumeric characters collapsed into a single hyphen and no leading or trailing hyphens. `slugify("Hello, World!")` returns `"hello-world"`. Covered by tests in `src/index.test.ts`.

- Added `slugify` export in `src/index.ts` using lowercase + trim, a `[^a-z0-9]+` -> `-` replacement, and leading/trailing hyphen stripping
